1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:07,285
Why do processor reviews test games at 1080p on the fastest graphics card they can get?

2
00:00:07,565 --> 00:00:08,689
It's on purpose.

3
00:00:09,439 --> 00:00:13,534
Each frame, the processor goes first, then the graphics card draws it.

4
00:00:13,814 --> 00:00:15,846
The slower one sets your frame rate.

5
00:00:16,596 --> 00:00:24,992
With an RTX 3060, TechSpot found a Core i9 just 3 percent faster than a budget Core i3.

6
00:00:25,273 --> 00:00:28,978
The graphics card was the wall, so both processors waited.

7
00:00:29,728 --> 00:00:34,783
Swap in an RTX 4090 and the gap jumps to 82 percent.

8
00:00:35,063 --> 00:00:39,285
That's 186 frames per second against 102.

9
00:00:40,035 --> 00:00:45,039
Low resolution on a huge graphics card gets the GPU out of the way.

10
00:00:45,319 --> 00:00:50,587
What's left is the processor's real ceiling, the one you'll hit after your next upgrade.

11
00:00:51,337 --> 00:00:55,012
The full breakdown is in our video, Bottlenecks Explained.

